WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.184
A flame graph needs recorded profile
stacks. Select the

00:00:03.184 --> 00:00:06.310
profiling result from the workload that
produced them,

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.436
then inspect the visible call paths and
their weights.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:13.920
The horizontal weight represents the
profile's sampled activity according to

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.330
that collector. It is not an independent
timing measurement of each function.

00:00:18.461 --> 00:00:22.381
An operation that appears in a wide stack
is a place to investigate,

00:00:22.381 --> 00:00:25.897
especially when it aligns with the
question and workload, but

00:00:25.897 --> 00:00:29.298
the graph does not establish a speedup for
a proposed edit.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.077
Follow the available source information to
inspect the operation and its inputs.

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:38.254
Use the Julia debugger for state or
correctness questions when helpful, then

00:00:38.254 --> 00:00:42.194
collect performance evidence separately
from stepping through the program.

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:47.046
For allocation views, check whether the
report contains totals or sampled sites.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:51.944
For wall profiles, remember that waiting
can be part of the recorded task behavior.

00:00:52.076 --> 00:00:54.240
The check guide explains the boundary and

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.721
provider requirements for each kind of
profile.
